  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 301.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 301.01 Purpose. The purpose of these rules is to prevent and minimize contamination of the land and waters of the state due to the improper storage and handling of oil as defined in RSA 146-A:2, III, which includes motor fuels, heating oils, lubricating oils, insulating oils, used oils, other petroleum products, and petroleum-contaminated liquids, by establishing criteria and procedures for the registration of aboveground oil storage facilities and standards for the design, installation, operation, maintenance, and monitoring of such facilities.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
